 **Inputs and Outputs:**
-*   **Input:** A tensor of coordinates $\mathbf{x} \in \mathbb{R}^{B \times D}$, where $B$ is the batch size and $D$ is the spatial dimensionality (typically 2 or 3). Values are expected to be normalized to the range $[0, 1]$ [S5, S11, S14, unofficial].
-*   **Output:** A tensor of encoded features $\mathbf{y} \in \mathbb{R}^{L \times B \times C}$, where $L$ is the number of resolution levels and $C$ is the number of feature channels per level [S5, S11, S14, unofficial]. Optionally, the gradient of the output with respect to the input $\frac{\partial \mathbf{y}}{\partial \mathbf{x}} \in \mathbb{R}^{B \times L \times D \times C}$ is computed [S12, S14, unofficial] (or flattened to $[B, L \cdot D \cdot C]$ [S5, S11, unofficial]).
